I was having the same problem and got this to work by editing the subread source code in the file 'input-files.c' and then recompiling.
Change the line:
pairer -> input_buff_SBAM_size = max(bin_buff_size_per_thread * 1024 * 1024,  100+FC_LONG_READ_RECORD_HARDLIMIT);

to:
pairer -> input_buff_SBAM_size = max(bin_buff_size_per_thread * 1024 * 1024 *10,  100+FC_LONG_READ_RECORD_HARDLIMIT);

Multiplying this variable by 10 might be a bit of overkill, but I successfully ran 'featureCounts' on the wheat genome, which is 17Gb in size and has 735943 contigs, using 500Gb of RAM.
Hope this helps.
Best wishes,
Graham

